# Expo / React Native doctrine

- Only `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` values may exist client-side. Never embed a Supabase
  `service_role` key, a Stripe `sk_live_` or `whsec_` secret, or a Twilio
  auth token in the app — those belong only in Edge Functions / server-side
  code.
- Store session tokens in `expo-secure-store`, chunking values past 2048
  bytes (SecureStore has a per-item size limit on some platforms). Never use
  `AsyncStorage` for session/auth tokens on native.
- Validate every environment variable and every Edge Function response with
  Zod before trusting its shape.
- Row Level Security (RLS) is the real authorization boundary. Client-side
  filtering is a UX nicety, never a security control — assume any client
  query can be replayed with arbitrary parameters.
- Every query must be scoped by `tenant_id` (or the tenant-equivalent key) —
  do not rely on the client to only ask for its own tenant's data.
- Every screen must explicitly handle all four states: loading, empty,
  error, and success. No screen may silently render nothing for a state it
  didn't anticipate.
- Every `FlatList` needs a stable `keyExtractor` (not array index unless the
  list is provably static).
- No placeholder screens and no dead buttons — every interactive element
  must do the thing it claims to do.
- The gate for this app is `tsc --noEmit` plus lint. Both must pass before
  reporting mobile work as done.
